WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:01.201
We've got good news.

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:04.504
We've got this focus, Speaker McCarthy.

00:00:05.305 --> 00:00:05.905
And we've reached

00:00:05.905 --> 00:00:08.308
the bipartisan budget agreement

00:00:08.308 --> 00:00:09.442
that we're ready to move

00:00:09.442 --> 00:00:11.277
to the full Congress

00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:12.779
and I think is a really important

00:00:12.779 --> 00:00:14.347
step forward. Excuse me.

00:00:14.347 --> 00:00:15.648
And it takes

00:00:15.648 --> 00:00:16.783
the threat of catastrophic

00:00:16.783 --> 00:00:18.518
to fall off the table.

00:00:18.518 --> 00:00:19.519
Protects our hard

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:22.088
earned and historic economic recovery.

00:00:22.088 --> 00:00:22.856
And the agreement

00:00:22.856 --> 00:00:24.324
also represents a compromise,

00:00:24.324 --> 00:00:25.358
which means no one got

00:00:25.358 --> 00:00:27.093
everything they want.

00:00:27.093 --> 00:00:29.162
But that's the responsibility

00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:30.430
of governing.

00:00:30.430 --> 00:00:32.665
And now this deal is good news for

00:00:32.665 --> 00:00:34.200
I believe you'll see

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:35.969
for the American people,

00:00:35.969 --> 00:00:36.870
the agreement prevents

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:38.671
the worst possible crisis.

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:39.739
And default

00:00:39.739 --> 00:00:40.473
for the first time

00:00:40.473 --> 00:00:42.008
in our nation's history.

00:00:42.008 --> 00:00:43.877
An economic recession.

00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:45.678
Retirement accounts devastated.

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:47.647
Millions of jobs lost.

00:00:47.647 --> 00:00:49.616
It also protects key priorities

00:00:49.616 --> 00:00:51.084
and accomplishments and values

00:00:51.084 --> 00:00:52.719
that congressional Democrats

00:00:52.719 --> 00:00:53.686
and I have fought long

00:00:53.686 --> 00:00:54.387
for long

00:00:54.387 --> 00:00:54.721
and hard

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:57.390
for investing in America's agenda.

00:00:57.624 --> 00:00:59.926
That's creating good jobs and communities

00:00:59.926 --> 00:01:01.294
throughout the country.

00:01:01.294 --> 00:01:02.362
Protect Social Security,

00:01:02.362 --> 00:01:04.364
Medicare and veterans, and so much more.

00:01:05.131 --> 00:01:06.433
The speaker and I made it

00:01:06.433 --> 00:01:07.801
clear from the start

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:08.868
that the only way forward

00:01:08.868 --> 00:01:11.071
was a bipartisan agreement.

00:01:11.071 --> 00:01:11.905
That agreement now

00:01:11.905 --> 00:01:13.907
goes to the United States House

00:01:14.140 --> 00:01:15.542
and to the Senate.

00:01:15.542 --> 00:01:17.343
I strongly urge both

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:19.579
both chambers to pass that agreement.

00:01:19.579 --> 00:01:20.747
Let's keep moving forward

00:01:20.747 --> 00:01:22.115
on meeting our obligations

00:01:22.115 --> 00:01:24.150
and building the strongest economy

00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:25.518
in the history of the world.

00:01:25.518 --> 00:01:26.753
I'll take a few questions.

00:01:27.821 --> 00:01:28.188
President,

00:01:28.188 --> 00:01:29.222
you said at the beginning

00:01:29.222 --> 00:01:31.324
that the deficit is not negotiable.

00:01:31.324 --> 00:01:32.959
Isn't that what you've just done here?

00:01:32.959 --> 00:01:35.161
Isn't that what you guys can't negotiate?

00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:36.896
Here's the deal.

00:01:36.896 --> 00:01:38.565
They passed they said they're going to

00:01:38.565 --> 00:01:40.333
they pass the debt ceiling

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:40.967
and they said

00:01:40.967 --> 00:01:42.368
they would only do it on condition

00:01:42.368 --> 00:01:44.871
that it have all these cuts in it.

00:01:44.871 --> 00:01:46.306
I said, I'm not going to do that.

00:01:46.306 --> 00:01:48.374
You pass the debt ceiling period.

00:01:48.908 --> 00:01:51.077
I'll negotiate with you on the cuts,

00:01:51.077 --> 00:01:52.145
what you say.

00:01:52.145 --> 00:01:54.514
What's going to happen with the budget's

00:01:54.514 --> 00:01:55.648
going to look like

00:01:55.648 --> 00:01:57.684
that's what we are to go know

00:01:57.684 --> 00:01:58.118
in order

00:01:58.118 --> 00:01:59.652
to get to

00:01:59.652 --> 00:02:00.854
them deciding

00:02:00.854 --> 00:02:01.988
that they're going to

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:04.858
go along with a new debt ceiling meeting

00:02:04.858 --> 00:02:06.926
that is not attached to something

00:02:06.926 --> 00:02:08.294
totally different attached.

00:02:08.294 --> 00:02:09.863
It was attached before.

00:02:09.863 --> 00:02:11.131
Suppose you want to try to make it

00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:12.732
look like I made some compromise

00:02:12.732 --> 00:02:14.501
on the debt ceiling and I didn't.

00:02:14.501 --> 00:02:16.169
I made a compromise on the budget.

00:02:17.170 --> 00:02:17.837
That's what they wanted

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:19.272
is you make a compromise on the budget

00:02:19.272 --> 00:02:20.039
and that's what you've got,

00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:20.874
even though you haven't gone

00:02:20.874 --> 00:02:21.741
as far as they wanted.

00:02:21.741 --> 00:02:23.643
Isn't that sure? Yeah.

00:02:23.643 --> 00:02:26.546
Well, I can think of an alternative

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:28.948
but the president.

00:02:28.948 --> 00:02:29.549
What do you say to

00:02:29.549 --> 00:02:30.850
members of your own party

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:31.718
who say you need

00:02:31.718 --> 00:02:33.953
to make concessions in this deal?

00:02:33.953 --> 00:02:35.855
Well, find I didn't

00:02:36.289 --> 00:02:36.589
Mr.

00:02:36.589 --> 00:02:37.457
President, on your

00:02:37.457 --> 00:02:39.259
on your allies and adversaries

00:02:39.259 --> 00:02:39.993
to America,

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:40.894
would you be willing to say

00:02:40.894 --> 00:02:41.728
about what you think

00:02:41.728 --> 00:02:43.062
this process said

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:44.631
to those adversaries and allies?

00:02:44.631 --> 00:02:45.665
We have a deal now,

00:02:45.665 --> 00:02:47.567
but what does the process say?

00:02:47.567 --> 00:02:48.935
What does the struggle process?

00:02:48.935 --> 00:02:50.970
We've been through this more than once,

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:52.639
and it's just the nature of the way

00:02:52.639 --> 00:02:55.441
we handle the deficit and handle

00:02:55.441 --> 00:02:57.544
whether we're going to each year going to

00:02:58.244 --> 00:02:59.612
pay our debts.

00:02:59.612 --> 00:03:00.680
And it's happened

00:03:00.680 --> 00:03:01.848
more than once

00:03:01.848 --> 00:03:03.249
will probably happen again.

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:04.217
But it's not going to happen

00:03:04.217 --> 00:03:06.286
at least for another two years here.

00:03:06.286 --> 00:03:07.287
And I don't think beyond

00:03:07.287 --> 00:03:09.589
I think beyond that it won't either.

00:03:09.589 --> 00:03:10.723
Do you think it's time for the U.S.

00:03:10.723 --> 00:03:12.091
to get rid of the debt limit

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:13.259
that this is, you know,

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:13.526
for that

00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:14.460
for the reasons you just laid out?

00:03:15.929 --> 00:03:17.063
No, I think you would

00:03:17.063 --> 00:03:18.464
cause more controversy

00:03:18.464 --> 00:03:19.832
getting rid of the debt limit,

00:03:19.832 --> 00:03:21.234
although I do.

00:03:21.234 --> 00:03:24.070
I am exploring the idea that we would

00:03:24.304 --> 00:03:25.705
at a later date,

00:03:25.705 --> 00:03:27.240
the year or two from now, decide

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:28.241
whether or not

00:03:28.241 --> 00:03:29.309
the 14th Amendment,

00:03:29.309 --> 00:03:31.611
how that actually would impact

00:03:31.611 --> 00:03:33.746
on whether or not you need to do

00:03:33.746 --> 00:03:35.248
the debt limit every year.

00:03:35.248 --> 00:03:37.217
But that's another day Mr.

00:03:37.217 --> 00:03:38.318
President, do you believe

00:03:38.318 --> 00:03:39.986
Speaker McCarthy has the votes

00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:42.655
and did he negotiate in good faith?

00:03:42.655 --> 00:03:44.057
I think he negotiated with me in

00:03:44.057 --> 00:03:44.557
good faith.

00:03:44.557 --> 00:03:45.792
He kept his word.

00:03:45.792 --> 00:03:46.893
He said what he would do.

00:03:46.893 --> 00:03:48.728
He did do what he said he'd do.

00:03:48.728 --> 00:03:50.763
And I have no idea at that.

00:03:50.763 --> 00:03:52.565
I expect he does,

00:03:52.565 --> 00:03:53.533
but I don't think

00:03:53.533 --> 00:03:55.268
he would have made the agreement.

00:03:55.268 --> 00:03:55.501
Mr.

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:56.636
President, do you have a

00:03:56.636 --> 00:03:57.003
do you have any

00:03:57.003 --> 00:03:59.038
comment on the elections in Turkey?

00:03:59.038 --> 00:04:01.241
Have you spoken with President Erdogan?

00:04:01.274 --> 00:04:03.042
I have not spoken to him yet.

00:04:03.042 --> 00:04:05.311
Do you wish you had a common money

00:04:05.878 --> 00:04:06.512
hard saying

00:04:06.512 --> 00:04:07.280
that his

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:08.081
policy will lead

00:04:08.081 --> 00:04:09.249
some people to go hungry?

00:04:09.249 --> 00:04:11.217
What is your response to that

00:04:11.217 --> 00:04:12.885
ridiculous assertion?

00:04:12.885 --> 00:04:13.319
Do you wish

00:04:13.319 --> 00:04:15.421
you started getting a petition sooner?

00:04:15.421 --> 00:04:17.557
No. The main difference, Mr.

00:04:17.557 --> 00:04:18.224
President, is

00:04:18.224 --> 00:04:21.027
financial aid for Ukraine secured in

00:04:21.194 --> 00:04:21.961
your new budget.

00:04:25.031 --> 00:04:25.298
Okay.

00:04:25.298 --> 00:04:25.932
There you have

00:04:25.932 --> 00:04:28.201
President Biden speaking to reporters

00:04:28.201 --> 00:04:30.036
just a few moments ago.

00:04:30.036 --> 00:04:32.171
He was saying essentially there

00:04:32.171 --> 00:04:33.206
that he believes

00:04:33.206 --> 00:04:34.140
that the House speaker, Kevin

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:34.574
McCarthy,

00:04:34.574 --> 00:04:35.408
was negotiating

00:04:35.408 --> 00:04:38.344
in good faith during this process.

00:04:38.344 --> 00:04:39.145
At one point,

00:04:39.145 --> 00:04:40.013
I think you were sparring

00:04:40.013 --> 00:04:41.014
with Peter Baker

00:04:41.014 --> 00:04:42.148
of The New York Times

00:04:42.148 --> 00:04:43.349
a bit there and said, well,

00:04:43.349 --> 00:04:45.184
what's the alternative

00:04:45.184 --> 00:04:47.220
when it comes to negotiating or not

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:49.489
negotiating over the debt ceiling?

00:04:49.756 --> 00:04:50.757
Let me go to you,

00:04:50.757 --> 00:04:52.292
Congresswoman Debbie Wasserman Schultz.

00:04:52.292 --> 00:04:53.426
And I interrupted you,

00:04:53.426 --> 00:04:54.694
although I did warn you in advance

00:04:54.694 --> 00:04:56.396
that that might happen.

00:04:56.596 --> 00:04:57.630
Your response

00:04:57.630 --> 00:04:59.832
to what the president had exactly.

00:05:00.166 --> 00:05:00.700
Your response

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:01.868
to what the president had to say there,

00:05:01.868 --> 00:05:03.703
because he was reminded

00:05:03.703 --> 00:05:04.771
of the fact that he did say

00:05:04.771 --> 00:05:05.738
he didn't want to negotiate

00:05:05.738 --> 00:05:06.539
over the debt ceiling

00:05:06.539 --> 00:05:07.674
and then he had a negotiator

00:05:07.674 --> 00:05:08.408
over the debt ceiling.

00:05:08.408 --> 00:05:09.475
That's when he said, well,

00:05:09.475 --> 00:05:11.411
what's the alternative there?

00:05:11.411 --> 00:05:12.712
It sounds as though

00:05:12.712 --> 00:05:13.379
the president,

00:05:13.379 --> 00:05:15.515
the White House Democrats really just

00:05:15.515 --> 00:05:16.482
didn't have a choice here.

00:05:16.482 --> 00:05:17.650
You had to negotiate over

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:18.251
the debt ceiling

00:05:21.187 --> 00:05:22.622
Well, you know,

00:05:22.622 --> 00:05:23.690
I was pleased that

00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:24.490
right from the beginning

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:26.059
of the discussions they took,

00:05:26.059 --> 00:05:26.759
whether or not

00:05:26.759 --> 00:05:27.960
we were going to raise the debt

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:29.095
ceiling and crash

00:05:29.095 --> 00:05:31.030
our economy off the table.

00:05:31.030 --> 00:05:32.031
Both sides agreed

00:05:32.031 --> 00:05:33.232
we're not going to do that.

00:05:33.232 --> 00:05:34.367
And then I mean, Jim,

00:05:34.367 --> 00:05:35.301
you know, as a longtime

00:05:35.301 --> 00:05:36.469
member of the Appropriations Committee,

00:05:36.469 --> 00:05:36.936
I can tell you

00:05:36.936 --> 00:05:38.071
this is the time of year

00:05:38.071 --> 00:05:39.472
when we are negotiating

00:05:39.472 --> 00:05:41.507
the appropriations top lines anyway.

00:05:41.541 --> 00:05:42.442
Essentially,

00:05:42.442 --> 00:05:43.209
we did that,

00:05:43.209 --> 00:05:43.743
you know, more

00:05:43.743 --> 00:05:45.011
at the beginning of the process

00:05:45.011 --> 00:05:46.479
through these negotiations.

00:05:46.479 --> 00:05:47.180
And that's what we talked

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:48.214
about on our caucus.

00:05:48.214 --> 00:05:49.215
This now

00:05:49.582 --> 00:05:51.584
We probably would have not wanted to get

00:05:51.984 --> 00:05:52.552
as much

00:05:52.552 --> 00:05:55.221
in the weeds in terms of the framework

00:05:55.722 --> 00:05:56.823
at this point in the game.

00:05:56.823 --> 00:05:58.791
But we had a lot at stake

00:05:58.825 --> 00:06:00.026
and it's really critical.

00:06:00.026 --> 00:06:00.927
We had Republicans

00:06:00.927 --> 00:06:03.029
who were willing to crash our economy

00:06:03.029 --> 00:06:04.163
into the side of a cliff,

00:06:04.163 --> 00:06:06.766
who were willing to not pay our bills,

00:06:06.766 --> 00:06:08.101
by the way, on a deficit

00:06:08.101 --> 00:06:10.136
that they ran up themselves.

00:06:10.136 --> 00:06:14.674
They have a $1.3 trillion unpaid

00:06:14.941 --> 00:06:16.642
bill of tax cuts

00:06:16.642 --> 00:06:17.944
that they wouldn't touch,

00:06:17.944 --> 00:06:19.746
mostly that went to millionaires

00:06:19.746 --> 00:06:20.947
and wealthy people.

00:06:20.947 --> 00:06:22.982
And that was off limits

00:06:22.982 --> 00:06:24.217
in those discussions,

00:06:24.217 --> 00:06:25.585
which is outrageous.

00:06:25.585 --> 00:06:26.052
I mean,

00:06:26.052 --> 00:06:27.687
when you have tax cuts,

00:06:27.687 --> 00:06:28.821
you're pulling revenue out of

00:06:28.821 --> 00:06:30.123
the economy. And

00:06:31.357 --> 00:06:33.426
that counts just as much as spending.

00:06:33.426 --> 00:06:35.194
And the Republicans under Donald Trump

00:06:35.194 --> 00:06:36.629
didn't pay for any of that.

00:06:36.629 --> 00:06:38.398
So they took that off the table.

00:06:38.398 --> 00:06:40.500
We were operating in a situation

00:06:40.500 --> 00:06:42.101
where we had to protect veterans funding

00:06:42.101 --> 00:06:43.503
if they were willing to cut.

00:06:43.503 --> 00:06:44.437
We had to make sure

00:06:44.437 --> 00:06:45.271
that we were going to have

00:06:45.271 --> 00:06:46.706
the kind of funding needs

00:06:46.706 --> 00:06:47.974
that were not supposed

00:06:47.974 --> 00:06:48.641
draconian

00:06:48.641 --> 00:06:50.343
from the cuts that they proposed.

00:06:50.343 --> 00:06:52.712
We ended up at FY 23 levels.

00:06:53.012 --> 00:06:54.313
The Republicans are trying to spin it.

00:06:54.313 --> 00:06:55.548
Is that by 22?

00:06:55.548 --> 00:06:56.883
But I know the details

00:06:56.883 --> 00:06:58.951
and I know the granularity of it

00:06:59.585 --> 00:07:00.686
at the end of the day

00:07:00.686 --> 00:07:01.921
when we go through the appropriations

00:07:01.921 --> 00:07:03.890
process will be at 23 levels.

00:07:03.890 --> 00:07:05.725
And by the way, we're protecting

00:07:05.725 --> 00:07:06.592
and ensuring

00:07:06.592 --> 00:07:08.060
that we don't go through this again

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:09.395
and next year.

00:07:09.395 --> 00:07:10.163
A quick, quick

00:07:10.163 --> 00:07:11.330
follow up on on

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:12.365
what the President had to say.

00:07:12.365 --> 00:07:13.833
Congresswoman, right there

00:07:13.833 --> 00:07:15.902
at the very end he indicated that

00:07:16.269 --> 00:07:19.005
maybe not before the 20, 24 election,

00:07:19.005 --> 00:07:20.740
maybe it's after the 20, 24 election.

00:07:20.740 --> 00:07:21.541
It sounds like he's

00:07:21.541 --> 00:07:23.643
going to be revisiting the idea

00:07:24.177 --> 00:07:25.445
of the 14th Amendment

00:07:25.445 --> 00:07:26.212
and whether or not

00:07:26.212 --> 00:07:26.813
the President

00:07:26.813 --> 00:07:28.915
can essentially raise the debt ceiling

00:07:28.915 --> 00:07:30.183
himself or herself

00:07:31.984 --> 00:07:34.253
by virtue of the 14th Amendment.

00:07:34.253 --> 00:07:35.922
Did you pick up on that

00:07:35.922 --> 00:07:36.656
when he said that?

00:07:36.656 --> 00:07:37.623
And what are your thoughts?

00:07:37.623 --> 00:07:37.890
Is it

00:07:37.890 --> 00:07:39.759
time for the United States

00:07:39.759 --> 00:07:40.526
to have a system

00:07:40.526 --> 00:07:42.361
where you don't have to go

00:07:42.361 --> 00:07:43.329
through the Congress

00:07:43.329 --> 00:07:44.931
to raise the debt ceiling?

00:07:44.931 --> 00:07:45.965
It sounds like the president said

00:07:45.965 --> 00:07:47.500
that would be too disruptive right now,

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:48.100
but it sounds like

00:07:48.100 --> 00:07:50.503
he is receptive to that idea perhaps

00:07:51.671 --> 00:07:52.472
down the road.

00:07:52.472 --> 00:07:54.106
What did you make of that?

00:07:55.508 --> 00:07:57.176
Well, I personally have always thought

00:07:57.176 --> 00:07:58.311
we should take off the table

00:07:58.311 --> 00:07:58.911
whether or not

00:07:58.911 --> 00:08:00.313
we pay our bills,

00:08:00.313 --> 00:08:01.214
that our nation,

00:08:01.214 --> 00:08:02.849
our debts, that our nation is a.

00:08:02.849 --> 00:08:03.916
There's no family in America

00:08:03.916 --> 00:08:04.784
that has the ability

00:08:04.784 --> 00:08:05.952
to not pay their bills.

00:08:05.952 --> 00:08:08.421
They can't just decide not to do that,

00:08:08.421 --> 00:08:09.522
and neither can we.

00:08:09.522 --> 00:08:10.957
And that shouldn't be subject

00:08:10.957 --> 00:08:12.358
to the political whims

00:08:12.358 --> 00:08:15.995
or the hostage taking ability of one side

00:08:15.995 --> 00:08:16.496
or the other.

00:08:16.496 --> 00:08:16.996
In this case,

00:08:16.996 --> 00:08:18.397
the Republicans are always

00:08:18.397 --> 00:08:19.499
the ones that are repeatedly

00:08:19.499 --> 00:08:20.433
willing to do that

00:08:20.433 --> 00:08:22.001
and hold the gun to the nation's

00:08:22.001 --> 00:08:23.503
the head of the nation's economy.

00:08:23.503 --> 00:08:24.470
I do think we should take

00:08:24.470 --> 00:08:25.104
that off the table,

00:08:25.104 --> 00:08:26.138
although I've heard the president

00:08:26.138 --> 00:08:28.441
say that it wouldn't be responsible,

00:08:29.175 --> 00:08:30.042
and I thought he meant

00:08:30.042 --> 00:08:31.077
it wouldn't be responsible

00:08:31.077 --> 00:08:32.845
to eliminate the debt ceiling.

00:08:32.845 --> 00:08:34.213
So I'm not really clear.

00:08:34.213 --> 00:08:35.114
I wasn't quite clear

00:08:35.114 --> 00:08:36.182
what he was saying, but

00:08:37.183 --> 00:08:38.417
I know he wasn't wanting to

00:08:38.417 --> 00:08:39.118
go through

00:08:39.118 --> 00:08:40.052
the 14th Amendment

00:08:40.052 --> 00:08:40.920
with the potential

00:08:40.920 --> 00:08:42.922
for judicial challenges now.

00:08:42.922 --> 00:08:44.257
And perhaps he would revisit

00:08:44.257 --> 00:08:45.525
that down the road.

00:08:45.525 --> 00:08:46.325
But at the end of the day,

00:08:46.325 --> 00:08:47.393
we have to pay our bills.

00:08:47.393 --> 00:08:48.928
We shouldn't be going,

00:08:49.529 --> 00:08:50.563
yeah, we can't have a default.

00:08:50.563 --> 00:08:51.664
That would be catastrophic.

00:08:51.664 --> 00:08:52.999
And even we can.

00:08:52.999 --> 00:08:53.499
Let me since

00:08:53.499 --> 00:08:55.501
you're right here in the studio with me,

00:08:55.501 --> 00:08:56.702
your thoughts on

00:08:56.702 --> 00:08:58.104
what the president had had to say.

00:08:58.104 --> 00:08:59.238
What stood out to you?

00:08:59.238 --> 00:09:00.840
He said that he believes the House

00:09:00.840 --> 00:09:02.208
speaker, Kevin McCarthy,

00:09:02.208 --> 00:09:04.410
is negotiating in good faith.

00:09:05.044 --> 00:09:05.912
That may not sit

00:09:05.912 --> 00:09:07.647
well with a lot of

00:09:07.647 --> 00:09:09.815
McCarthy's Republican, very conservative

00:09:09.815 --> 00:09:11.551
Republican colleagues

00:09:11.551 --> 00:09:12.552
who wish

00:09:12.552 --> 00:09:13.586
that McCarthy had gotten

00:09:13.586 --> 00:09:14.787
more out of this.

00:09:14.787 --> 00:09:15.821
But this is always

00:09:15.821 --> 00:09:17.723
who President Biden has been.

00:09:17.723 --> 00:09:19.926
He is always a creature of the Senate.

00:09:19.926 --> 00:09:23.162
He's always been this pragmatic lawmaker

00:09:23.162 --> 00:09:23.930
moderate,

00:09:23.930 --> 00:09:26.198
willing to work with Republicans.

00:09:26.198 --> 00:09:27.033
You know, when I saw him

00:09:27.033 --> 00:09:27.533
come out,

00:09:27.533 --> 00:09:28.334
I thought

00:09:28.334 --> 00:09:30.169
this makes it all the more hard

00:09:30.169 --> 00:09:31.871
for Republicans to argue

00:09:31.871 --> 00:09:33.773
that he is beholden to the left.

00:09:33.773 --> 00:09:34.974
Clearly, he is not

00:09:34.974 --> 00:09:36.409
if he is willing to make

00:09:36.409 --> 00:09:37.710
these compromises.

00:09:37.710 --> 00:09:40.112
But it was a reversal, to be clear, Jim,

00:09:40.112 --> 00:09:41.714
he said all along

00:09:41.714 --> 00:09:43.249
I have argued that the only way

00:09:43.249 --> 00:09:44.951
forward is a bipartisan agreement.

00:09:44.951 --> 00:09:46.485
He has not said that all along.

00:09:46.485 --> 00:09:47.753
That is incorrect.

00:09:47.753 --> 00:09:49.255
He initially said that

00:09:49.255 --> 00:09:51.157
that this was non-negotiable.

00:09:51.157 --> 00:09:53.192
Well, he negotiated

00:09:53.192 --> 00:09:55.595
and he yeah, he long said there would be

00:09:55.661 --> 00:09:56.996
should be no compromise

00:09:56.996 --> 00:09:58.531
when it comes to the debt ceiling,

00:09:58.531 --> 00:10:00.900
that this is obligatory,

00:10:00.900 --> 00:10:02.234
that this is the responsibility

00:10:02.234 --> 00:10:03.269
of Congress

00:10:03.269 --> 00:10:06.305
So ultimately, he did have to compromise.

00:10:06.305 --> 00:10:07.740
But I don't know

00:10:07.740 --> 00:10:10.142
how much of a political liability

00:10:10.142 --> 00:10:10.743
it is for him

00:10:10.743 --> 00:10:12.178
because it robs Republicans

00:10:12.178 --> 00:10:13.346
of a talking point

00:10:13.346 --> 00:10:15.481
that he is totally dictated

00:10:15.481 --> 00:10:17.183
by progressives in the left flank.

